DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES
The Municipal Manager shall be the Administrative Head of the Municipality and shall report to the Municipal Board and be responsible for the following functions:
Act on behalf of the Municipal Board ensuring the execution of the decisions of the board;
Prepare and present for approval to the Board of the Municipality, an annual estimate of revenue and expenditure;
Be principally responsible for building and maintaining a strong alliance and effective working relationships between the Board and the civil society, private sector, and community-based organizations;
Prepare, and submit to the Board an annual report on the activities and accomplishments of the departments and agencies comprising the executive branch of the board;
Act as an ex-officio member of all committees of the Board;
Exercise supervision over all departments and agencies of the Municipality and coordination of its activities;
Administer and enforce all Municipality By-laws, resolutions, franchises, leases, contracts, permits, and othe Municipality decisions;
Prepare and administer the annual Municipality budget;
Administer Municipality utilities and property;
Encourage and support regional and intergovernmental cooperation;
Promote cooperation among the Board of the Municipality, staff, and citizens in developing Municipality policies and building a sense of community, and
Perform any other duties as directed by the Board of the Municipality.
REQUIREMENTS FOR APPOINTMENT
Subject to Article 232 of the Constitution, a person shall qualify to be appointed as city or Municipal Manager if the Person; -
Is a citizen of Kenya
Holds a degree from a university recognized in Kenya or its equivalent;
Has proven experience of not less than five (5) years in administration or management either in the public or private sector; and
Be ordinarily a resident or have a permanent dwelling within the County.
Be holder of a Senior Management Course training from Kenya School of Government

Objective of the Consultancy:
The overall objective of the consultancy is to support the implementation of the Health & Safety (H&S) Support Service by:
Creating comprehensive, country-specific H&S Handbooks tailored to minigrid developers operating in Nigeria, Zambia, and Kenya;
Training and building the capacity of AMDA staff to support H&S compliance and awareness among members;
Developing and setting up a virtual Minigrid H&S Help Desk.
Scope of Work
The consultant's scope of work will encompass the following activities, aligned with the project's components:
H&S Country Handbooks
Develop three comprehensive handbooks (one each for Nigeria, Zambia, and Kenya), including:
Overview of country-specific H&S laws and regulatory frameworks;
Sector-specific risks and mitigation practices;
Compliance checklists and templates;
Case studies and success stories (where applicable);
Incorporate insights from the H&S protocol mapping exercise.
Ensure content is accessible, practical, and aligned with national licensing requirements for minigrids.
Collaborate with the AMDA Communications team for final formatting and design.
Capacity Building
Design and deliver training modules for AMDA staff on:
National and regional H&S regulations relevant to minigrids;
Best practices in incident reporting, compliance monitoring, and mitigation;
Use of the Minigrid Help Desk platform and resource materials;
Support AMDA staff in becoming H&S focal points within their regions.
Conduct virtual and/or in-person workshops and create a training manual or toolkit.
Development of the Minigrid H&S Help Desk
Design and structure the Help Desk interface and workflow (in collaboration with AMDA’s technical team).
Define standard operating procedures (SOPs) for handling inquiries, referrals, and incident reporting.
Create a database of certified H&S consultants for referrals.
Provide technical documentation and guidance for future updates and maintenance.
Consultant Qualifications
The ideal consultant will possess the following qualifications and experience:
Technical Expertise:
Minimum of 7 years of experience and demonstrated expertise in Health and Safety (H&S) regulations, protocols, and best practices, particularly within the energy or infrastructure sectors;
Experience with DRE solutions, minigrids, or off-grid energy technologies is highly desirable;
Knowledge of H&S regulatory landscapes in Sub-Saharan African countries, specifically Nigeria, Zambia, and Kenya, is a significant advantage

Job Summary:
The successful candidates will be reporting to the Dean School of Pharmacy and Health Sciences, the incumbent will be expected to teach, selected course in Human Anatomy including, Gross Anatomy, Embryology and Histology,
Key Responsibilities
Teach and assess selected Anatomy courses to undergraduate students in Bachelor of Science Nursing and Bachelor of Pharmacy
Introduce and mark practical reports for assigned courses that have practical component
Perform any other duties as may be assigned from time to time.
Support and mentor students in their career endeavors.
Participate in curriculum development activities to ensure that the programs and the teaching content are up-to-date and marketable;
Participate in program assessment and reviews;
Minimum Educational Qualifications and Professional Experience
A Master of science degree in Human Anatomy, Bachelor of Medicine and Bachelor of surgery, Bachelor of Pharmacy, Bachelor of Clinical Medicine, Bachelor of Nursing or any related discipline from recognized/accredited university.
A PhD in Human Anatomy from recognized/accredited university will be an added advantage.
Should have at least three (3) years of University teaching experience
Been registered by the relevant Professional Body
Personal Attributes & Competencies
Excellent computer background;
Be self-motivated and highly-disciplined;
Excellent command of the subject area including lesson planning;
Managing ambiguity and emotions;
Managing technological change;
Excellent communication skills;
Excellent listening and mediation skills;
Excellent fundraising and grants writing skills;
Excellent presentation skills;
Excellent research writing skills.

Key Responsibilities and Duties: -
Timely collection of company debt; Provision of supporting documents to facilitate the collection process (timely delivery of invoices, statements and demand notes); Maintain accurate and updated customers' statements; Work with the commercial team, legal office and external debt collectors to recover debts; Responding to client queries on time while ensuring customer satisfaction; Achievement of agreed targets; Strictly adhere to the company's credit control policy.
Qualifications, Experience, Skills & Attributes
: -
Bachelor's degree in Finance or its equivalent from a recognized institution; CPA (K) or ACCA Certification; Certificate in Credit Management(desirable); At least three (3) years'of debt collection experience with a proven track record; Strong networks across all business sectors;
Excellent interpersonal, communication and negotiation skills;
Excellent analytical skills; Ability to meet strict deadlines; Excellent IT skills;
High degree of integrity and honesty;
Result driven and a team player.

Position responsibilities:
Reviewing resources and familiarising themselves with ACLED guides, FAQs, and other materials;
Preparing for training and participating in training on the cleaning, review, and coding of data,as the role requires;
Reviewing news media and other source reports available online for information on violent conflict and political unrest in a set of allocated countries;
Monitoring the emergence of new actors, regimes, and significant political developments in a set of allocated countries, and proposing revisions to the project’s actor file and regime year’s database as required;
Managing and organizing regional desk files and documents;
Cleaning and organizing data lists, such as for regional actors and locations;
Undertaking general quality assurance tasks provided by the Research Manager;
Reviewing and integrating feedback into ongoing coding efforts and data work;
Assisting with data review and cleaning as required;
Contributing analytical content to the project’s reports, or other research if required;
Performing sourcing and coding work if needed;
Assisting with the management of the regional desk;
Filling in for the Research Manager when needed.
ACLED is seeking applicants who meet the following requirements:
Good understanding of ACLED methodology (essential);
Strong analytical and problem solving skills (essential);
Experience with management and providing feedback (preferred);
Solid understanding of Excel, including basic formulas, (essential) and Tableau (preferred);
Excellent command of English;
Experience working to deadlines with limited supervision;
A high level of attention to detail (essential) and ability to receive and incorporate feedback;
Research focus or professional experience in conflict research or peacebuilding (preferred).

Company Details:
The Media Council of Kenya is an independent national institution established by the Media Council Act 2013 for purposes of setting of media standards and ensuring compliance with those standards as set out in Article 34(5) of the Constitution and for connected purposes. The Council started as a sel...read moref-regulating body in 2004 to regulate media industry in Kenya but transited through the Media Act 2007 and adopted co-regulation media regulation approach, where board members and the Secretariat while receiving government funds to support some of its activities, remain very independent in their operations and are not subject to any form of control. 

 Vision

 A professional and free media accountable to the public.

 Mission

 To safeguard media freedom, enhance professionalism and arbitrate media disputes.

 Our Core Values

 The Council is committed to the following guiding principles:

 1. Integrity

 2. Independence

 3. Professionalism

 4. Transparency and Accountability

 Council’s Role, Mandate, Functions and Authority

The Council draws its mandate and authority from the Media Act 2013. Its functions are to:

Promote and protect the freedom and independence of the media;
Prescribe standards of journalists, media practitioners and media enterprises;
Ensure the protection of the rights and privileges of journalists in the performance of their duties;
Promote and enhance ethical and professional standards amongst journalists and media enterprises;
Advise the government or the relevant regulatory authority on matters relating to professional, education and the training of journalists and other media practitioners;
Set standards, in consultation with the relevant training institutions, for professional education and training of journalists;
Develop and regulate ethical and disciplinary standards for journalists, media practitioners and media enterprises;
Accredit journalists and foreign journalists by certifying their competence, authority or credibility against official standards based on the quality and training of journalists in Kenya including the maintaining of a register of journalists, media enterprises and such other related registers as it may deem fit and issuance of such document evidencing accreditation with the Council as the Council shall determine;
Conduct an annual review of the performance and the general public opinion of the media, and publish the results in at least two daily newspapers of national circulation;
Through the Cabinet Secretary, table before Parliament reports on its functions;
Establish media standards and regulate and monitor compliance with the media standards;
Facilitate resolution of disputes between the government and the media and between the public and the media and intra media;
Compile and maintain a register of accredited journalists, foreign journalists, media enterprises and such other related registers as it may consider necessary;
Subject to any other written law, consider and approve applications for accreditation by educational institutions that seek to offer courses in journalism; and
Perform such other functions as may be assigned to it under any other written law.
